      "findingMessages": {
        "doc-drift.corpus-sraw-allowlisted-though-decoded": "KNOWN_UNSUPPORTED still lists \"sraw\" as 'Canon sRAW / mRAW' not decoded, but cr2.rs now routes SRAW_TYPE=4 frames to vendor::cr2::sraw::decode, measured on the 31 CC0 sRAW/mRAW corpus samples. The corpus test accepts RawError::Unsupported for any file whose name contains 'sraw' (corpus.rs:87), so a regression that makes every sRAW/mRAW file Unsupported again passes the corpus gate silently instead of failing.",
        "doc-drift.raw-crate-doc-format-list-stale": "The crate-level 'Formats' list omits containers decode() supports (Samsung SRW, Hasselblad 3FR/FFF via RawFormat::CfaTiff, Kodak DCS via RawFormat::KodakDcs) and its 'can't decode yet' list names only compressed ORF and CR3 variants, while corpus.rs:16 points to 'the crate docs' for a list that also includes Nikon HE NEF. RawFormat::OtherTiff's doc (line 115) still lists 3FR among undecoded TIFF raws although CfaTiff (line 109-112) says 3FR/FFF are read by the DNG reader. A maintainer or user reading the docs gets the wrong support matrix.",
        "doc-drift.headless-painted-text-doc-misattached": "The doc line for painted_text ('Every piece of text the last frame painted...') sits above painted_shapes, so rustdoc shows painted_shapes as returning text in paint order and painted_text (line 191) has no doc at all; Headless::painted_text (line 295) links to HeadlessView::painted_text expecting that description."
      },
      "findingTitles": {
        "doc-drift.corpus-sraw-allowlisted-though-decoded": "Remove \"sraw\" from KNOWN_UNSUPPORTED (or narrow it to the specific non-YCbCr raw types still refused) so sRAW/mRAW corpus files must decode.",
